{"words":[{"id":4511,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::a::art","eng":"a","eng_normalized":"a","kk":"/ə/, /eɪ/","tense":"art.","ch":"[['一個']]","analysis":"不定冠詞，源自古英語 ān，意為「一」。用於單數可數名詞前，表示「一個」、「某個」、「任何一個」。","definition":"1. Used before singular countable nouns to refer to a non-specific or non-particular member of a group or category; 2. Used when mentioning something for the first time.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I saw a dog in the park.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我在公園裡看到了一隻狗。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a doctor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位醫生。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":37,"unit_name":"C3U10","source_id":4,"source_name":"文華高中-常春藤單字","chEntries":["一個"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":5353,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::abandon::v","eng":"abandon","eng_normalized":"abandon","kk":"əˈbændən","tense":"v.","ch":"[['拋棄'], ['放棄'], ['離棄']]","analysis":"此字源自古法語 abandonner，來自 an-（在……情況下）+ bandon（法語的控制權、禁止）。原始概念為「脫離控制」、「在沒有保護的情況下」。構詞上，a- 是加強語氣或表示「給予」的字首，bandon- 來自 banna（命令、禁止）。核心語意是「將某物置於無人管轄、無人保護的狀態」，引申為「拋棄」、「放棄」或「離棄」。","definition":"to give up completely a course of action, a practice, or a way of thinking; to cease to support or look after (someone); desert.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They had to abandon their car in the snow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們不得不把車子丟在雪中。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He decided to abandon his dreams of becoming a musician.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他決定放棄成為音樂家的夢想。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":57,"unit_name":"L1","source_id":5,"source_name":"龍騰課本","chEntries":["拋棄","放棄","離棄"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":5114,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::abnormal::adj","eng":"abnormal","eng_normalized":"abnormal","kk":"æbˈnɔːrməl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['反常的'], ['變態的'], ['不規則的']]","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 abnormalis，由 ab-（離開、遠離）+ norma（規則、標準）+ -al（形容詞字尾）組成。ab- 來自印歐語系 *apo-，意為「離開、遠離」。norma 來自拉丁語，意為「角尺、規範、標準」，可能與 *ǵnō-（知道、辨認）有關。-al 是常見的拉丁形容詞字尾，用於將名詞轉為形容詞。核心語意為「偏離標準」或「不符合規則」，由此引申出「反常的、不尋常的、變態的」等義。","definition":"deviating from what is normal or usual; unusual; irregular; pathological.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His behavior was abnormal for a child his age.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的行為對他這個年紀的孩子來說很不尋常。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The test results showed some abnormal readings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"檢測結果顯示了一些異常讀數。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":52,"unit_name":"U62","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["反常的","變態的","不規則的"],"examMeaningIndexes":[0],"examMeaningTexts":["反常的"]},{"id":5115,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::abortion::n","eng":"abortion","eng_normalized":"abortion","kk":"əˈbɔːrʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['墮胎'], ['流產'], ['中止（計畫、活動）']]","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 abortio，由 abortire（過早生產、墮胎）演變而來。abortire 可能是由 ab-（離開、停止）+ ortus（出生、起源，來自 oriri「升起、開始」）組成，意為「未能順利出生」或「提早結束」。-ion 是拉丁語常見的名詞字尾，用於表示動作或狀態。核心語意為「事情的中止或失敗」，引申為「胎兒的墮落」或「計畫的取消」。","definition":"the termination of a pregnancy; the failure of a plan or project; a miscarriage.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The debate over abortion continues to be a sensitive issue.\",\n    \"ch\": \"關於墮胎的辯論仍然是一個敏感的問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project was an abortion from the start.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個專案從一開始就失敗了。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":52,"unit_name":"U62","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["墮胎","流產","中止"],"examMeaningIndexes":[0],"examMeaningTexts":["墮胎"]},{"id":4528,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::about::prep","eng":"about","eng_normalized":"about","kk":"/əˈbaʊt/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['關於'], ['大約'], ['在...周圍']]","analysis":"源自古英語 on bæftan，意為「在後面」。後來演變成表示「周圍」、「大概」、「關於」。核心語意從「圍繞」引申為「關於」。","definition":"1. On the subject of; concerning; 2. Approximately; 3. On all sides of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Tell me about your trip.\",\n    \"ch\": \"跟我說說你的旅行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's about ten o'clock.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大約十點鐘了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children were playing about the room.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們在房間裡玩耍。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":37,"unit_name":"C3U10","source_id":4,"source_name":"文華高中-常春藤單字","chEntries":["關於","大約","在...周圍"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":5116,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::abrupt::adj","eng":"abrupt","eng_normalized":"abrupt","kk":"əˈbrʌpt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['突然的'], ['粗魯的'], ['陡峭的']]","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 abruptus，是 ab-, abs-（離開、遠離）+ rumpere（弄斷、打破）的過去分詞。rumpere 來自印歐語系 *h₂rem-（停止、休息）或 *reup-（撕裂、拔出）。abruptus 的字面意思是「被弄斷的、被打破的」，引申為「突然發生的、急促的」。由此衍生出「出乎意料的、唐突的、不順暢的」。當用於人際互動時，表示「粗魯、生硬」；當用於地形時，表示「突然中斷、陡峭」。","definition":"sudden and unexpected; brief to the point of rudeness; steep or broken.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was an abrupt change in the weather.\",\n    \"ch\": \"天氣突然發生了變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave an abrupt answer and walked away.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他唐突地回答了一下就走開了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The road became abrupt at the cliff edge.\",\n    \"ch\": \"道路在懸崖邊變得陡峭。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":52,"unit_name":"U62","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["突然的","粗魯的","陡峭的"],"examMeaningIndexes":[0],"examMeaningTexts":["突然的"]},{"id":3197,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::abstract::adj","eng":"abstract","eng_normalized":"abstract","kk":"/ˈæbstrækt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['抽象的'], ['深奧的'], ['非實體的'], ['理論上的']]","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁文 'abstractus'，意為 'drawn away'，即分離、抽出。此字首 'abs-' 意為 'away'，'trahere' 意為 'to draw'。引申為非具體的、概念性的，與具體 'concrete' 相反。","definition":"1. existing in thought or as an idea but not having a physical or concrete existence; 2. relating to or involving general ideas or qualities rather than specific people, events, or things; 3. difficult to understand; abstruse; 4. (of art) not representing reality in a conventional way.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Love is an abstract concept.\",\n    \"ch\": \"愛是一個抽象的概念。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a very abstract way of thinking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的思考方式非常抽象。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book deals with abstract philosophical problems.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書探討抽象的哲學問題。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":24,"unit_name":"U41","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["抽象的","深奧的","非實體的","理論上的"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":3198,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::abstract::n","eng":"abstract","eng_normalized":"abstract","kk":"/ˈæbstrækt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['摘要'], ['概要'], ['抽象概念']]","analysis":"名詞形式，源自形容詞，指將事物的核心或主要觀點獨立出來，形成一個簡要的概述，如同將具體的內容提煉為抽象的重點。也指非具體的概念。","definition":"1. a summary of the contents of a book, article, or speech; 2. a piece of abstract art.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please read the abstract before the full paper.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請在閱讀整篇論文前先看摘要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist's latest work is an abstract.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位藝術家最新的作品是一件抽象畫。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":24,"unit_name":"U41","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["摘要","概要","抽象概念"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":3199,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::abstract::v","eng":"abstract","eng_normalized":"abstract","kk":"/æbˈstrækt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['提取'], ['抽取出'], ['摘要'], ['使抽象化']]","analysis":"動詞形式，強調將某事物（尤其是數據、思想或物質）從更廣泛的整體中分離出來，形成獨立的部分或概念。詞源同上，從 'drawn away' 引申為『抽出』。","definition":"1. to consider something theoretically or separately from something else; 2. to draw out or remove; 3. to make an abstract, summary, or digest of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is difficult to abstract meaning from such complex data.\",\n    \"ch\": \"很難從如此複雜的數據中提取出意義。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to abstract the key findings for the report.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要為報告提煉出關鍵發現。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The philosopher tried to abstract principles of morality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位哲學家試圖歸納出道德原則。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":24,"unit_name":"U41","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["提取","抽取出","摘要","使抽象化"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":5425,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::abundance::n","eng":"abundance","eng_normalized":"abundance","kk":"əˈbʌndəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['豐富'], ['充裕'], ['大量'], ['豐盛']]","analysis":"此字為派生詞，由形容詞 \"abundant\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ance\" 構成。\"abundant\" 源自拉丁語 \"abundans\"，是動詞 \"abundare\" 的現在分詞，意為\"充溢\"、\"豐富\"。\"abundare\" 由 \"ab-\" (離開、遠離，在此表示\"過多\"或\"溢出\") 和 \"undare\" (波浪般流動) 構成，\"undare\" 又源於 \"unda\" (波浪)。構詞上，\"ab-\" 提供了「過量」的語意，\"undare\" 提供了「流動」的圖像，整體表示「如波浪般湧出、充溢」。字尾 \"-ance\" 將形容詞的「充裕」狀態轉化為抽象名詞，表示「豐富」、「充裕」或「大量」的狀態或性質。","definition":"a large quantity of something; a great amount of something; plenty; profusion; more than enough.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The region is known for its abundance of natural resources.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該地區以其豐富的自然資源而聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was an abundance of food at the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"派對上有豐富的食物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The abundance of information online can be overwhelming.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網路上豐富的資訊可能會讓人不知所措。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":59,"unit_name":"L3","source_id":5,"source_name":"龍騰課本","chEntries":["豐富","充裕","大量","豐盛"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":5426,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::abundant::adj","eng":"abundant","eng_normalized":"abundant","kk":"əˈbʌndənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['豐富的'], ['充裕的'], ['大量的'], ['充足的']]","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"abundans\"，是動詞 \"abundare\" 的現在分詞，意為\"充溢\"、\"豐富\"。\"abundare\" 由 \"ab-\" (離開、遠離，在此表示\"過多\"或\"溢出\") 和 \"undare\" (波浪般流動) 構成，\"undare\" 又源於 \"unda\" (波浪)。構詞上，\"ab-\" 提供了「過量」的語意，\"undare\" 提供了「流動」的圖像，整體表示「如波浪般湧出、充溢」。\"Abundant\" 作形容詞，描述某物「極其豐富」、「充裕」或「大量存在」，遠超過所需。","definition":"existing or available in large quantities; plentiful; more than enough.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Fresh fruits are abundant in summer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"夏季水果供應充足。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The forest provides abundant opportunities for hiking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這片森林提供了豐富的健行機會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Natural gas is abundant in this region.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個地區天然氣儲量豐富。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":59,"unit_name":"L3","source_id":5,"source_name":"龍騰課本","chEntries":["豐富的","充裕的","大量的","充足的"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":5282,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::accelerate::v","eng":"accelerate","eng_normalized":"accelerate","kk":"əkˈsɛləˌreɪt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['加速', '加快'], ['（指運動、過程等）加速', '促進']]","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'accelerare'，由 'ad-'（朝向，表示增強）和 'celerare'（使快速）組成。'celerare' 又來自 'celer'（快速的）。構詞上，'ad-' 作為加強前綴，'celer' 為詞根，'-are' 為動詞後綴。原始語義即為「使快速」。在現代英語中，'accelerate' 主要用於描述速度、過程或進展的增長，由具體的「加快速度」引申為抽象的「促進」。","definition":"to speed up the progress of (something); to increase in speed; to happen or develop more quickly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new policy will accelerate economic growth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新政策將會加速經濟增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car accelerated rapidly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"汽車快速地加速了。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":56,"unit_name":"U63","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["加速","加快","促進"],"examMeaningIndexes":[0,2],"examMeaningTexts":["加速","促進"]},{"id":3259,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::accent::n","eng":"accent","eng_normalized":"accent","kk":"/ˈæksənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['口音；腔調'], ['強調；重音'], ['（尤指演講或寫作中的）標音符號']]","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'accentus'，意為「曲調，音調」，由 'ad-'（朝向）+ 'cantus'（歌唱，歌曲）組成。最初指音樂中的音調，後引申至語言中的語音特徵（口音、重音）以及書寫中表示重音的符號。","definition":"1. a distinct way of pronouncing a language, especially one that is characteristic of a particular country, region, or social group; 2. an emphasis given to a particular syllable or word in speech; 3. a mark written above a letter to indicate the pronunciation or stress of a syllable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She speaks with a strong Southern accent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她說話帶著濃重的南方口音。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The word 'father' has the accent on the first syllable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"單字 'father' 的重音在第一個音節。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The acute accent (´) is used in some languages.\",\n    \"ch\": \"銳音符號（´）在某些語言中使用。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":25,"unit_name":"U42","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["口音","腔調","強調","重音","標音符號"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":3260,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::accent::v","eng":"accent","eng_normalized":"accent","kk":"/əkˈsɛnt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['強調；著重'], ['加重音於...']]","analysis":"動詞形式，源自名詞 'accent'。強調某個詞或音節的發音或意義。與名詞的「重音」概念直接關聯。","definition":"1. to emphasize or stress a particular word, syllable, or sound; 2. to place an accent mark on (a letter or syllable).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He accented the last word of his speech for emphasis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在演講的最後一個詞上加重音以示強調。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The singer accented the high notes in the chorus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"歌手在副歌的高音處特別加重。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":25,"unit_name":"U42","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["強調","著重","加重音於..."],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":4616,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::acceptable::adj","eng":"acceptable","eng_normalized":"acceptable","kk":"/əkˈseptəbəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可接受的'], ['令人滿意的'], ['尚可的']]","analysis":"由 'accept' (接受) + '-able' (能夠...的) 組成。'Accept' 源自拉丁語 'accipere' (接受、拿到)。此字指事物達到某種最低標準，雖然不一定完美，但足以被容忍、接受或認為可以。","definition":"satisfactory or good enough; able to be accepted.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The proposal is acceptable to all parties.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項提議對所有相關方來說都是可以接受的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His performance was acceptable, but not outstanding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的表現尚可，但並不突出。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":31,"unit_name":"C3U16","source_id":4,"source_name":"文華高中-常春藤單字","chEntries":["可接受的","令人滿意的","尚可的"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":3261,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::accountant::n","eng":"accountant","eng_normalized":"accountant","kk":"/əˈkaʊntənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['會計師']]","analysis":"源自 'account' (帳目，敘述)，加上 '-ant'（從事某事的人）後綴。指專門負責管理和審核帳目的人。","definition":"a person whose job is to keep the financial accounts of a business and to check them.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I need to hire an accountant to help with my taxes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我需要聘請一位會計師來幫我處理稅務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's accountant discovered a discrepancy in the records.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司的會計師發現記錄中有出入。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":25,"unit_name":"U42","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["會計師"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":5283,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::accounting::n","eng":"accounting","eng_normalized":"accounting","kk":"əˈkaʊntɪŋ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['會計學'], ['會計工作', '帳務處理']]","analysis":"此字由動詞 'account' 加上名詞化後綴 '-ing' 構成。'account' 本身源自古法語 'aconter'（計算、敘述），由 'a-'（to）和 'conte'（計算，來自拉丁語 'computare'）組成。'accounting' 作為名詞，指代記錄、分類、匯總和解釋財務交易的系統或實踐。其核心語意是「計算」和「報告」，引申為「會計學」或「會計工作」。","definition":"the systematic recording, reporting, and analysis of the financial transactions of a business or organization; the profession or work of an accountant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is studying accounting at university.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她正在大學學習會計學。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company hired a new accountant to handle their accounting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司僱用了一位新會計師來處理他們的帳務。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":56,"unit_name":"U63","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["會計學","會計工作","帳務處理"],"examMeaningIndexes":[0],"examMeaningTexts":["會計學"]},{"id":5556,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::accuracy::n","eng":"accuracy","eng_normalized":"accuracy","kk":"ˈækjərəsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['精確度'], ['準確性'], ['正確性']]","analysis":"此字由 \"accurate\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-cy\" 構成。\"accurate\" 源自拉丁語 \"accurrere\"，意為 \"to run to, run up\"（跑到，跑近），由 \"ad-\"（to, toward，向，朝）和 \"currere\"（to run，跑）組成。\"accurrere\" 的引申義是指「達到目標」，因此 \"accurate\" 指「能夠精確地達到目標」或「符合標準」。\"-cy\" 是構成抽象名詞的字尾，表示「狀態、品質」。因此，\"accuracy\" 的核心語義是「達到目標、符合標準的品質或狀態」，即「精確性」或「準確性」。","definition":"1. The condition or quality of being accurate; freedom from error or defect; 2. The degree to which the result of a measurement, calculation, or specification conforms to the correct or a predicted result.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The accuracy of the data is crucial for our research.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些數據的準確性對我們的研究至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pilot maintained a high level of accuracy in navigation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"飛行員在導航中保持了高度的精確性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to ensure the accuracy of the translation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要確保翻譯的準確性。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":62,"unit_name":"L6","source_id":5,"source_name":"龍騰課本","chEntries":["精確度","準確性","正確性"],"examMeaningIndexes":[1],"examMeaningTexts":["準確性"]},{"id":4562,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::accurate::adj","eng":"accurate","eng_normalized":"accurate","kk":"/ˈækjərət/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['準確的', '精確的'], ['（陳述、測量等）正確的']]","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'accuratus'，'ad-' (to) 和 'cura' (care - 關心、小心) 的組合。核心概念是「非常小心地」進行，從而達到精確。\n    1. 準確的、精確的：指測量、數據、預測等非常接近真實值或目標。\n    2. 正確的：指陳述或判斷符合事實。","definition":"1. (of information, measurements, etc.) precise; exact.; 2. correct in all details; error-free.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report provided an accurate account of the events.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份報告提供了對事件的準確敘述。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His estimate of the cost was remarkably accurate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對費用的估計非常準確。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need accurate data to make a decision.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要準確的數據來做決定。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":38,"unit_name":"C3U11","source_id":4,"source_name":"文華高中-常春藤單字","chEntries":["準確的","精確的","正確的"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":5684,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::accusation::n","eng":"accusation","eng_normalized":"accusation","kk":"ˌækjuˈzeɪʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['指控'], ['控告'], ['指責']]","analysis":"此字由動詞 'accuse' 加上名詞化後綴 '-ation' 構成。'accuse' 源自古法語 acuser（來自拉丁語 causari，意為『爭論，引起訴訟』）。'-ation' 後綴用於將動詞轉化為名詞，表示動作、過程、狀態或結果。因此，'accusation' 指的就是「被指控的動作或陳述」，即「指控、控告」。核心語意是「提出某人有罪或有過失的言論」。","definition":"a charge or claim that someone has done something illegal or wrong; the act of accusing someone.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The accusation was never proven.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項指控從未被證實。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He faced a serious accusation of fraud.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他面臨嚴重的欺詐指控。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":65,"unit_name":"L9","source_id":5,"source_name":"龍騰課本","chEntries":["指控","控告","指責"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":5683,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::accuse::v","eng":"accuse","eng_normalized":"accuse","kk":"əˈkjuːz","tense":"v.","ch":"[['指控'], ['控告'], ['指責']]","analysis":"此字源自古法語 acuser，由 a-（來自拉丁語 ad-，表示『對……』）+ cuser（來自拉丁語 causari，意為『爭論，引起訴訟』，源自 causa，意為『原因，案件』）構成。構詞上，'a-' 指向的對象，'cuser' 則表示『提起訴訟』或『聲稱某事』。核心語意是「公開提出某人有罪的指控，或對某人的不當行為提出質疑」。語意演變從『爭論案件』到『提起訴訟』，再到『指控某人有罪』。","definition":"to claim that someone has done something illegal or wrong.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was accused of theft.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被指控偷竊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She accused him of lying.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她指責他撒謊。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":65,"unit_name":"L9","source_id":5,"source_name":"龍騰課本","chEntries":["指控","控告","指責"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":3920,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::achieve::v","eng":"achieve","eng_normalized":"achieve","kk":"/əˈtʃiːv/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['達成', '實現'], ['獲得']]","analysis":"源自古法語 'achever' (意為「完成、達到頂點」)，來自 'a-' (意為「到」) + 'chef' (意為「頭、頂」)。最初的意思是「達到頂峰」，引申為「完成、實現、達成目標」。","definition":"1. to succeed in doing or achieving something; 2. to obtain something, especially by effort.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She worked hard to achieve her goals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她努力工作以實現她的目標。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team achieved a remarkable victory.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支隊伍取得了一場了不起的勝利。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He finally achieved fame in his field.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他終於在他的領域獲得了名聲。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":29,"unit_name":"C3U2","source_id":4,"source_name":"文華高中-常春藤單字","chEntries":["達成","實現","獲得"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":5817,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::acknowledge::v","eng":"acknowledge","eng_normalized":"acknowledge","kk":"əkˈnɑlɪdʒ","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"承認\"  ],  [    \"認可\"  ],  [    \"告知\"  ],  [    \"表示收到\"  ]]","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 acknown（知道）加上ledge（承認），結合了「知道」與「承認」兩層含義。acknowledge 的核心構詞可追溯至古英語 'cnāwan'（知道）和 'lecgan'（放置、使……），意指「確認某事物已知」。詞源上，'a-' 是加強前綴，'know' 來自原始日耳曼語 *kannaną (to know)，'ledge' 則來自古英語 'lecgan' (to lay down, to cause to lie down)，與'lay' 同源。在語言演變中，'a-' 前綴加強了動詞的語意，'ledge' 演變成與承認、確認相關的意義。最初的語義是「確認某事已知的狀態」，進而引申出「承認」或「認可」某事實、聲明或權威。此外，'acknowledge' 也可用來表示「告知」收件人已收到訊息，這源於確認訊息已「被知道」的概念。更進一步，也可指「表示對某人的存在或地位的認可」，例如在社交場合。","definition":"1. To accept or admit the existence or truth of; to recognize the fact or importance of.; 2. To express recognition or appreciation of.; 3. To inform (someone) of the receipt of (a letter, message, etc.).; 4. To recognize the existence, presence, or fact of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has to acknowledge his mistakes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他必須承認他的錯誤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We acknowledge receipt of your order.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們謹此告知已收到您的訂單。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She acknowledged his efforts with a smile.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她以微笑認可了他的努力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The guard acknowledged the visitor with a nod.\",\n    \"ch\": \"守衛點頭表示認可訪客。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":66,"unit_name":"U58","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["承認","認可","告知","表示收到"],"examMeaningIndexes":[0,3],"examMeaningTexts":["承認","表示收到"]},{"id":5284,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::acquaint::v","eng":"acquaint","eng_normalized":"acquaint","kk":"əˈkweɪnt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['使認識', '使熟悉', '告知']]","analysis":"此字源自古法語 'acointier'，由 'a-'（to）和 'cointer'（使認識，可能來自中古拉丁語 'accognitare'，意為「變得熟悉」）。構詞上，'a-' 作為加強或使動前綴，'cointer' 為詞根。其原始語義為「使某人與某事或某人變得熟悉」。現代英語中的 'acquaint' 常與介詞 'with' 連用，表示「使熟悉某事物」或「告知某事」。","definition":"to make someone aware of or familiar with something; to introduce to someone.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I need to acquaint myself with the new procedures.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我需要熟悉新的流程。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was acquainted with the facts of the case.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他了解案情的實情。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":56,"unit_name":"U63","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["使認識","使熟悉","告知"],"examMeaningIndexes":[0,1],"examMeaningTexts":["使認識","使熟悉"]},{"id":5337,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::acquire::v","eng":"acquire","eng_normalized":"acquire","kk":"əˈkwaɪər","tense":"v.","ch":"[['獲得'], ['學到'], ['購得']]","analysis":"此字源自古法語 aquerre，來自拉丁語 adquirere，由 ad-（朝向、加上）+ quirere（尋找、獲得）組成， quirere 為 quaerere（尋找、詢問）的變體。構詞上，ad- 表示「朝向」，quir- 是字根，表示「尋找、獲得」。原始語意為「主動尋找並獲得」。現代語意涵蓋「透過努力或購買獲得」、「學到（知識、技能）」等。","definition":"to gain something by purchase or by birth, or by effort, skill, or the like; to learn or develop a skill or habit.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He managed to acquire a valuable collection of stamps.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他設法獲得了大量珍貴的郵票收藏。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children acquire language naturally.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兒童能自然地學到語言。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":57,"unit_name":"L1","source_id":5,"source_name":"龍騰課本","chEntries":["獲得","學到","購得"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":6060,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::acquisition::n","eng":"acquisition","eng_normalized":"acquisition","kk":"ˌækwəˈzɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"獲得\"  ],  [    \"收購\"  ],  [    \"購得物\"  ],  [    \"習得\"  ],  [    \"掌握\"  ]]","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 acquirere（acquire），由 ad-（towards, to）和 quaerere（to seek, to ask for）組成。在此作名詞，指「獲得」這個動作或狀態，以及「被獲得的東西」。構詞上，-ition 是常見的名詞後綴，將動詞變為表示動作或結果的名詞。核心語義是用力去尋求、獲取並最終得到。在商業語境中，尤其指「收購」一家公司或資產，成為「購得物」。在心理學或教育學中，則指知識、技能的「習得」或「掌握」。","definition":"1. the act or process of acquiring or obtaining something; 2. something that is acquired or obtained, especially a company or asset; 3. the process or skill of learning or developing something, such as a language or a skill.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The acquisition of new skills is essential for career growth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"獲得新技能對職業發展至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's latest acquisition was a small tech firm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司的最新收購是一家小型科技公司。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Language acquisition can be challenging for young children.\",\n    \"ch\": \"語言習得對幼兒來說可能很有挑戰性。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":67,"unit_name":"U64","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["獲得","收購","購得物","習得","掌握"],"examMeaningIndexes":[0],"examMeaningTexts":["獲得"]},{"id":5338,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::acquisition::n","eng":"acquisition","eng_normalized":"acquisition","kk":"ækˈwɪzɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['獲得'], ['收購'], ['收購物']]","analysis":"此字由動詞 acquire 加上名詞字尾 -ition 構成。acquire 源自古法語 aquerre，來自拉丁語 adquirere（尋找、獲得）。-ition 是拉丁語的抽象名詞字尾，表示「行為、狀態或結果」。因此，acquisition 的核心語意為「獲得的行為或結果」，引申為「獲得某物（尤指較大的物品，如公司）」或「收購」。","definition":"an act of acquiring or gaining possession; something that is acquired, especially a company or property bought by another company.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's latest acquisition has increased its market share.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司最新的收購增加了其市場佔有率。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The acquisition of new skills is crucial for career growth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"獲得新技能對職業發展至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":57,"unit_name":"L1","source_id":5,"source_name":"龍騰課本","chEntries":["獲得","收購","收購物"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":6061,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::activist::n","eng":"activist","eng_normalized":"activist","kk":"ˈæktəvɪst","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"行動主義者\"  ],  [    \"活動家\"  ],  [    \"積極分子\"  ]]","analysis":"此字由 active（活躍的）加上名詞後綴 -ist（從事某種活動或信仰的人）構成。Active 源自拉丁語 activus，意為「活動的，活躍的」，本身來自 act-（to do, to act）。Activist 指的是一個積極參與某項政治或社會事業，並採取實際行動來推動變革的人。核心語義是「積極採取行動去倡導或反對某事的人」。","definition":"a person who campaigns to bring about political or social change, especially through direct action.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a well-known environmental activist.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位知名的環保活動家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The group of activists staged a protest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那群活動家發起了抗議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He became a peace activist after the war.\",\n    \"ch\": \"戰後他成為了一名和平主義者。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":67,"unit_name":"U64","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["行動主義者","活動家","積極分子"],"examMeaningIndexes":[2],"examMeaningTexts":["積極分子"]},{"id":3898,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::actually::adv","eng":"actually","eng_normalized":"actually","kk":"/ˈæktʃuəli/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['實際上', '事實上'], ['真的', '確實']]","analysis":"由 'actual' (實際的) 加上副詞後綴 '-ly' 組成。核心是「依據事實」。用來強調某事物是真實的，與預期或表面情況不同，或用來引出真實情況。","definition":"1. in fact; in reality. 2. used to emphasize a statement or to correct a misconception.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I thought he was joking, but he was actually serious.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我以為他在開玩笑，但他實際上是認真的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What actually happened was different.\",\n    \"ch\": \"實際上發生的情況是不同的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's actually quite a simple process.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這實際上是一個相當簡單的過程。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":28,"unit_name":"C3U1","source_id":4,"source_name":"文華高中-常春藤單字","chEntries":["實際上","事實上","真的","確實"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":6062,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::acute::adj","eng":"acute","eng_normalized":"acute","kk":"əˈkjut","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"尖銳的\"  ],  [    \"敏銳的\"  ],  [    \"嚴重的\"  ],  [    \"急性的\"  ]]","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 acutus，意為「尖的，銳利的」，是動詞 acuere（to sharpen）的過去分詞。構詞上，ac- 來自 acu-，意為「尖、銳利」，-ute 是形容詞後綴。此字的核心語義與「尖銳」相關，引申出多種含義：物理上的「尖銳」形狀；感知上的「敏銳」；情況上的「嚴重」或「劇烈」；醫學上的「急性」發作。這些義項都體現了「程度極高」或「非常明顯」的特點。","definition":"1. sharp or penetrating, especially in intellect, perception, or physical appearance (e.g., an acute angle); 2. (of a bad situation or feeling) intense; severe; 3. (of a disease or condition) of sudden onset, sharp rise, and short course.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The triangle has an acute angle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個三角形有一個銳角。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has an acute sense of smell.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有靈敏的嗅覺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The situation is becoming increasingly acute.\",\n    \"ch\": \"局勢正變得日益嚴峻。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She suffers from acute appendicitis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她患有急性闌尾炎。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":67,"unit_name":"U64","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["尖銳的","敏銳的","嚴重的","急性的"],"examMeaningIndexes":[2,3],"examMeaningTexts":["嚴重的","急性的"]},{"id":3121,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::addict::v","eng":"addict","eng_normalized":"addict","kk":"/əˈdɪkt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['使沉迷；使對...上癮'], ['（非正式）使沉迷於']]","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'addicere'，意為「授予，歸屬」。'ad-'（朝向）+ 'dicere'（說，宣告）。最初表示將某物「歸還」給某人，引申為將某人「歸屬」於某種習慣或愛好。現代用法中，'addict' 作動詞時，強調的是使人對某物產生強烈依賴或沉迷，特別是藥物、行為或事物。","definition":"1. to cause someone to become addicted to a substance or activity; 2. to make someone unable to stop doing something that is bad for them.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new video game is so addictive, many people stay up all night playing it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這款新的電子遊戲太容易讓人上癮了，很多人玩到半夜都不睡覺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He became addicted to gambling.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他染上了賭博的惡習。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":23,"unit_name":"U40","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["使沉迷","使對...上癮","使沉迷於"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":3122,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::addict::n","eng":"addict","eng_normalized":"addict","kk":"/ˈædɪkt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['癮君子；對...有強烈癮頭的人'], ['（非正式）熱衷者']]","analysis":"此為名詞用法，源自動詞 'addict'。指代被某種物質（如毒品、酒精）或活動（如賭博、網路）嚴重依賴或沉迷的人。'addict' 的核心概念是「被某物牢牢抓住、無法擺脫」。","definition":"1. a person who is addicted to a particular substance or activity; 2. an enthusiast or devotee of a particular activity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization provides support for former drug addicts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該組織為前吸毒癮君子提供支援。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She's a total coffee addict; she needs at least three cups a day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是個徹頭徹尾的咖啡愛好者；她每天至少需要三杯咖啡。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":23,"unit_name":"U40","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["癮君子","對...有強烈癮頭的人","熱衷者"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":3123,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::addicted::adj","eng":"addicted","eng_normalized":"addicted","kk":"/əˈdɪktɪd/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['上癮的；沉迷的']]","analysis":"這是動詞 'addict' 的過去分詞，用作形容詞。表示某人處於對某種物質或活動上癮或極度沉迷的狀態。其語意直接承襲了動詞『使沉迷』的概念，強調結果。","definition":"physically or mentally dependent on a particular substance or activity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He admitted he was addicted to video games.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他承認自己對電子遊戲上癮了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt miserable and withdrawn, clearly addicted to her medication.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她感到痛苦且孤僻，顯然對她的藥物上癮了。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":23,"unit_name":"U40","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["上癮的","沉迷的"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":5604,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::addition::n","eng":"addition","eng_normalized":"addition","kk":"əˈdɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['加法'], ['增加'], ['添加物']]","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'additio'，由動詞 'addere'（添加）派生，'addere' 由 'ad-'（向）和 'dare'（給予）組成。構詞學上，它是由動詞 'add'（添加）加上名詞化後綴 '-tion' 所構成。'-tion' 字尾常將動詞轉換為表示「行動」、「過程」或「結果」的名詞。原始語意是「給予」或「添加」，演變為「加法」（數學上的）、「增加的行為或過程」，以及「被添加的物品」。","definition":"1. The action or process of adding something to something else; 2. The process of adding up numbers; 3. A thing added to something else.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The addition of a new wing significantly increased the museum's exhibition space.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新翼樓的增加顯著擴大了博物館的展覽空間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children are learning basic addition in school.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們正在學校學習基本的加法。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new feature is a welcome addition to the software.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項新功能是該軟體一個受歡迎的補充。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":63,"unit_name":"L7","source_id":5,"source_name":"龍騰課本","chEntries":["加法","增加","添加物"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":4006,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::additional::adj","eng":"additional","eng_normalized":"additional","kk":"/əˈdɪʃənl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['額外的', '附加的']]","analysis":"由 'add' (增加) 和 '-itional' (形容詞詞尾) 組成。指在原有基礎上增加的、額外的。","definition":"added to an existing or usual amount or number; extra.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You may need additional blankets.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你可能需要額外的毯子。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":30,"unit_name":"C3U3","source_id":4,"source_name":"文華高中-常春藤單字","chEntries":["額外的","附加的"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":5605,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::additional::adj","eng":"additional","eng_normalized":"additional","kk":"əˈdɪʃənəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['額外的'], ['附加的'], ['額外增加的']]","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'additio'（添加），經由 'additus'（添加，過去分詞）派生。構詞學上，它是由名詞 'addition'（增加、添加）加上形容詞化後綴 '-al' 所形成。'-al' 字尾通常將名詞轉換為形容詞，表示「與……有關的」或「屬於……的」。因此，'additional' 的核心語意是「與添加或增加有關的」，引申為「額外的」、「附加的」、「另外的」。","definition":"1. Added to something else; extra; 2. Existing or happening in addition to something else.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please provide any additional information you may have.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請提供您可能擁有的任何額外資訊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"An additional charge will be applied for express delivery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"快遞將收取額外費用。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":63,"unit_name":"L7","source_id":5,"source_name":"龍騰課本","chEntries":["額外的","附加的","額外增加的"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":5603,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::additionally::adv","eng":"additionally","eng_normalized":"additionally","kk":"əˈdɪʃənəli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['此外'], ['而且'], ['另外']]","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'additio'，意為「添加」，由 'addere'（添加）派生而來。構詞上，'addition' 是核心名詞（意為「加法」或「添加物」），加上了形容詞化後綴 '-al'，成為 'additional'（附加的），最後再接副詞化後綴 '-ly'，形成副詞 'additionally'。'-ly' 後綴將形容詞轉換為副詞，表示「以……的方式」或「具有……的性質」。'additional' 的「附加的」語意，透過 '-ly' 轉化為副詞，表示「額外地」、「此外」。原始語意是「增加的、額外的」，在副詞形式中，它用於引入額外的資訊或論點。","definition":"1. In addition; also; 2. Furthermore.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hotel offers free breakfast; additionally, guests can use the gym.\",\n    \"ch\": \"飯店提供免費早餐；此外，客人還可以使用健身房。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a talented musician and, additionally, a skilled writer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位才華橫溢的音樂家，而且，他也是一位技巧嫻熟的作家。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":63,"unit_name":"L7","source_id":5,"source_name":"龍騰課本","chEntries":["此外","而且","另外"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":4569,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::admire::v","eng":"admire","eng_normalized":"admire","kk":"/ədˈmaɪər/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['欽佩', '讚賞'], ['欣賞', '仰慕']]","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'admirari'，'ad-' (to) 和 'mirari' (to wonder at - 驚奇、讚嘆)。核心概念是因某人的優點、成就或特質而感到驚嘆和讚賞。\n    1. 欽佩、讚賞：指對某人的品德、能力或成就給予高度評價。\n    2. 欣賞、仰慕：指欣賞美麗的事物、景色或某人，帶有讚美的意味。","definition":"1. regard with respect or warm approval.; 2. look at with pleasure; find beautiful or delightful.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I truly admire your courage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我真心欽佩你的勇氣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She admired the stunning view from the mountaintop.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她欣賞山頂上壯麗的景色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many people admire his dedication to his work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多人讚賞他對工作的投入。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":38,"unit_name":"C3U11","source_id":4,"source_name":"文華高中-常春藤單字","chEntries":["欽佩","讚賞","欣賞","仰慕"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":5543,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::admit::v","eng":"admit","eng_normalized":"admit","kk":"ədˈmɪt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['承認'], ['允許進入'], ['接納']]","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'admittere'，由 'ad-' (to) + 'mittere' (to send, to let go) 構成。原始語義是「讓……進去」或「允許……進入」。構詞上，'ad-' 表示「朝向、到……」，'mit-' 是 'mittere' 的詞幹，意為「派遣、發送、讓」。'admit' 的核心語義是「讓某事物或某人進入」，這引申出兩大類含義：1. 允許進入（場所、組織）；2. 承認（錯誤、事實）。後者是從「讓事實進入你的認知」或「讓真相被承認」演變而來。","definition":"to confess to be true or to be the case, typically with reluctance; to allow (someone) to enter a place or organization.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He admitted that he had made a mistake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他承認自己犯了錯誤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hospital can admit up to 200 patients.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家醫院最多可以接納 200 名病人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was admitted to the university.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她被大學錄取了。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":61,"unit_name":"L5","source_id":5,"source_name":"龍騰課本","chEntries":["承認","允許進入","接納"],"examMeaningIndexes":[0],"examMeaningTexts":["承認"]},{"id":5818,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::adore::v","eng":"adore","eng_normalized":"adore","kk":"əˈdɔr","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"崇拜\"  ],  [    \"熱愛\"  ],  [    \"非常喜歡\"  ],  [    \"崇敬\"  ]]","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'adorare'，由 'ad-' (to, toward) 和 'orare' (to speak, to pray) 構成。'Orare' 本意為「說話」，引申為「祈禱」，因為祈禱通常涉及向神明「訴說」。'Ad-' 在此表示「向……」，因此 'adorare' 的字面意思是「向……祈禱」，進而發展出「崇拜」、「敬拜」的意思。在拉丁語晚期及中古英語中，'adore' 被引入，用以表達對神聖事物的極度尊敬與愛慕。現代語義則進一步擴展，不僅限於宗教崇拜，也可指對某人或某物表達極度的愛意、熱情和欣賞，常帶有浪漫或極端喜愛的色彩。更深一層，亦可指「極度崇敬」。","definition":"1. To worship or revere; to regard with deep love and respect.; 2. To love or like very much.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She adored her grandmother.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她非常愛戴她的祖母。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fans adored the singer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"粉絲們崇拜這位歌手。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He adores classical music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他熱愛古典音樂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They adored the idea of a perfect life.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們崇敬完美生活的想法。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":66,"unit_name":"U58","source_id":1,"source_name":"字彙王","chEntries":["崇拜","熱愛","非常喜歡","崇敬"],"examMeaningIndexes":[0,1],"examMeaningTexts":["崇拜","熱愛"]},{"id":3978,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::advantage::n","eng":"advantage","eng_normalized":"advantage","kk":"/ədˈvæntɪdʒ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['優勢', '有利條件'], ['好處']]","analysis":"詞源：古法語 'avantage' (優勢)，來自拉丁文 'ab-' (離開) 和 'vantage' (有利的地位)。引申為「使人處於有利地位」或「因處於有利地位而獲得的好處」。","definition":"1. a condition or circumstance that puts one in a stronger position relative to others; 2. a condition or situation that is favourable or gives one a lead.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her height gives her an advantage in basketball.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的身高讓她在籃球上佔有優勢。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The advantage of this plan is its simplicity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個計畫的好處在於它的簡單性。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":30,"unit_name":"C3U3","source_id":4,"source_name":"文華高中-常春藤單字","chEntries":["優勢","有利條件","好處"],"examMeaningIndexes":[],"examMeaningTexts":[]},{"id":5460,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::adventure::n","eng":"adventure","eng_normalized":"adventure","kk":"ædvɛnˈtʃɜr","tense":"n.","ch":"[['冒險'], ['奇遇'], ['歷險']]","analysis":"此字源自古法語 'aventure'，意指「機遇、事件、奇遇」。'Aventure' 又來自拉丁語 'adventura'，字面意思是「將要發生的事」，'ad-' 是「朝向」的意思，'ventura' 是 'venire'（來）的將來分詞。在中古英語中，'adventure' 最初常用來指「意外的事件」或「幸運的機會」，後來逐漸演變成「充滿刺激、危險或新奇的經歷」。核心語意是「未知的、可能充滿挑戰或驚喜的事件或經歷」。","definition":"1. An unusual and exciting or daring experience or activity.; 2. A commercial enterprise undertaken with the hope of succeeding.; 3. A series of exciting or unusual events or experiences.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He sought adventure in far-off lands.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他到遠方尋求冒險。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The novel tells the story of a young explorer's adventure in the jungle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本小說講述了一位年輕探險家在叢林中的冒險故事。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was an adventure to travel without any plans.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沒有任何計劃的旅行是一場冒險。\"\n  }\n]","unit_id":60,"unit_name":"L4","source_id":5,"source_name":"龍騰課本","chEntries":["冒險","奇遇","歷險"],"examMeaningIndexes":[0,2],"examMeaningTexts":["冒險","歷險"]}],"totalGroups":1654,"loadedGroups":36,"hasMore":true,"nextOffset":36,"pageOffset":0,"targetWordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::abandon::v"}